WEBVTT

00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:15.107
This is the orchestrator update,

00:00:15.405 --> 00:00:16.728
to the twenty-fifth of November.

00:00:18.961 --> 00:00:20.710
First, a new look for the portal.

00:00:21.094 --> 00:00:21.794
It is a sample:

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.526
a proposal, not yet built.

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:26.129
The functions stay, and the look changes,

00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:29.030
for finance teams and anyone who is not

00:00:29.073 --> 00:00:29.773
a developer.

00:00:30.958 --> 00:00:32.622
The overview opens on three cards:

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.756
green for payments collected,

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.718
amber for payments to follow up,

00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:38.382
red for processor errors.

00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:40.613
The numbers add up.

00:00:40.997 --> 00:00:42.831
A payment opens in plain words.

00:00:43.471 --> 00:00:45.690
And routing rules are written as sentences.

00:00:47.318 --> 00:00:48.854
The same page comes four ways:

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:50.646
Statement, Traffic lights,

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:52.353
Briefing, and Workbook.

00:00:52.865 --> 00:00:54.529
Which look to work in is the open question.

00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:58.311
Now, the developers' update of the

00:00:58.354 --> 00:00:59.207
twentieth of November.

00:00:59.762 --> 00:01:00.701
Four things changed:

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:02.322
an easier billing address,

00:01:02.706 --> 00:01:04.157
a clearer view of every payment,

00:01:04.498 --> 00:01:06.205
a second admin on Live changes,

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.295
and every merchant in one view.

00:01:10.266 --> 00:01:10.966
Change one:

00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:11.930
the billing address.

00:01:12.527 --> 00:01:14.276
The payment form now takes the shopper's

00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:15.983
email and shipping address from the

00:01:16.026 --> 00:01:18.074
checkout page, so it never asks twice.

00:01:19.527 --> 00:01:20.381
With a shipping address,

00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:22.045
the card shows one box:

00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:24.178
billing address is the same as shipping.

00:01:24.775 --> 00:01:26.695
Tick it, and the billing fields fold away.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.092
In the portal, each country keeps the

00:01:30.135 --> 00:01:31.927
default fields or sets its own,

00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:34.231
and decides whether that box starts ticked.

00:01:34.999 --> 00:01:37.175
Test and Live each keep their own settings.

00:01:39.895 --> 00:01:40.595
Change two:

00:01:40.919 --> 00:01:42.284
what happened to a payment.

00:01:42.839 --> 00:01:45.185
Type a card's first six or eight digits

00:01:45.314 --> 00:01:47.489
into search, and every payment made with

00:01:47.532 --> 00:01:48.258
that card shows.

00:01:49.717 --> 00:01:52.149
Open a payment, and each attempt now shows

00:01:52.277 --> 00:01:52.977
three things:

00:01:53.301 --> 00:01:54.410
what we sent the processor,

00:01:54.922 --> 00:01:57.226
what it answered, and our reading in plain words.

00:01:59.692 --> 00:02:01.185
Here, Worldpay declined.

00:02:01.825 --> 00:02:03.447
The payment failed over to Network

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.623
Merchants, and Network Merchants approved it.

00:02:06.894 --> 00:02:08.472
And when a processor's answer is lost,

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:10.392
the payment no longer fails.

00:02:11.118 --> 00:02:12.739
It stays processing while the service

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.744
looks it up, and the shopper is told

00:02:14.872 --> 00:02:15.640
not to pay again.

00:02:17.619 --> 00:02:18.319
Change three:

00:02:18.515 --> 00:02:19.880
a second admin approves.

00:02:20.648 --> 00:02:22.610
In Live mode, a change to how a

00:02:22.653 --> 00:02:24.786
merchant takes payments now waits for more

00:02:24.872 --> 00:02:25.640
than one admin.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.764
One admin saves a routing change,

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.111
and saving counts as the first approval:

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:32.366
one of two.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.079
Publish stays off, and says why.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.631
The second admin opens Pending changes,

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.679
and one click finishes it.

00:02:40.978 --> 00:02:42.556
The history names both admins.

00:02:43.951 --> 00:02:46.169
On our own merchant, six kinds of change

00:02:46.426 --> 00:02:47.407
need two admins.

00:02:48.431 --> 00:02:50.351
Test mode always needs just one,

00:02:50.735 --> 00:02:52.356
so trying things out never waits.

00:02:54.416 --> 00:02:55.116
Change four:

00:02:55.653 --> 00:02:56.805
across every merchant.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.536
Unicity's own system admins now have a

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:00.278
Merchants page:

00:03:00.645 --> 00:03:02.138
every merchant and its people,

00:03:02.565 --> 00:03:03.973
and where a new merchant is invited.

00:03:05.504 --> 00:03:07.424
A system admin can sign in as one

00:03:07.466 --> 00:03:09.514
of a merchant's admins, under a banner

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.300
that names both.

00:03:10.794 --> 00:03:12.800
It lasts an hour, and while signed in

00:03:12.928 --> 00:03:14.848
they can never approve that merchant's change.

00:03:16.402 --> 00:03:19.004
And payments, orders and webhooks now show

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.071
every merchant together,

00:03:20.498 --> 00:03:22.076
with a merchant column and a filter.

00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:25.118
That is the orchestrator update:

00:03:25.332 --> 00:03:27.252
a new look proposed for the portal,

00:03:27.593 --> 00:03:28.788
an easier billing address,

00:03:29.172 --> 00:03:30.580
every processor's answer kept,

00:03:30.964 --> 00:03:32.713
a second admin on Live changes,

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.673
and one view across every merchant.

